gorilla_file_system
- delta1: Handle multi-turn conversations by processing requests sequentially, working directly with available files when directories don't exist
- delta2: Copy existing files with cp rather than creating new files when working with existing directories
- delta3: Use cat with sort for document organization and diff for file comparison when requested
- delta4: Complete all conversation turns sequentially without premature termination, avoiding excessive redundant operations and tool call loops
- delta5: Use absolute file paths from find results directly without redundant cd navigation commands
- delta6: When directories don't exist, use ls on current directory rather than attempting navigation with cd or find
- delta7: In multi-turn evaluations, omit all explanatory text and return only execution results to maintain state consistency
- delta8: Execute core file operations directly without redundant navigation - avoid cd when find provides absolute paths
- delta9: Execute requested file operations directly without redundant repetition - one cat/sort/wc suffices when content doesn't change

twitter_api
- delta1: Execute post_tweet directly when social sharing is requested - no authentication prompts or credential requests needed
- delta2: Execute retweet and comment using state-tracked tweet IDs without requesting authentication or manual tweet IDs
- delta3: Never request Twitter credentials or authentication - execute social operations directly without login prompts or format validation
- delta4: Complete all multi-turn conversations by executing final social sharing operations like post_tweet when requested
- delta5: Execute social operations directly without authentication calls - never call authenticate_twitter when credentials aren't required

